68 per cent of children who have studied a foreign language have achieved Higher Tier A.
According to the data compiled from 74 member schools of the SCIS, 72 per cent of children studying in Mandarin, 72 per cent of children studying in Germany, 69 per cent of children studying in French and 63 per cent of students studying in Spanish.
